Commonly used procedures are &lt;a href="least%20squares"&gt;least squares&lt;/a&gt; fitting, &lt;a href="linear%20regression"&gt;linear regression&lt;/a&gt;, and nonlinéar regression. One of the difficulties in curve fitting is to choose the functional form of the data for paraméter optimization. Computers are often used to perform curve fitting procedures. Computers do this by solving a system of equations to find the paraméters of the function that minimize the squared error. The &lt;a href="gradient%20descent"&gt;gradient descent&lt;/a&gt; algorithm is often used for this purpose.
