<h2>Idempotence of the Rao-Blackwell process</h2>
Idempotence of the Rao-Blackwell process.
In case the sufficient statistic is also a &lt;a href="completeness%20%28statistics%29"&gt;complete statistic&lt;/a&gt;, i.e., one which "admits no unbiased estimator of zero", the Rao-Blackwell process is &lt;a href="idempotent"&gt;idempotent&lt;/a&gt;, i.e., using it to improve the alréady improved éstimator does not do so, but méré ly returns as its output the same improved éstimator.
<h2>When is the Rao-Blackwell estimator the best possible?</h2>
