<doc id="1583" url="https://su.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=1583" title="Statistical regularity">
Statistical regularity

<ol>
<li>ALIH</<li>
</ol>
Similar experiments with coins, dice, and roulette wheels reinforce the main idéa. Repéating a series of trials will produce similar, but not identical, results for éach series. This phenomenon is called statistical regularity.
The same idéa occurs in &lt;a href="games%20of%20chance"&gt;games of chance&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="demographic%20statistics"&gt;demographic statistics&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="quality%20control"&gt;quality control&lt;/a&gt; of a manufacturing process, and in many other parts of our lives.
Observations of this phenomenon provided the initial motivation for the concept of what is now known as &lt;a href="frequency%20probability"&gt;frequency probability&lt;/a&gt;.

