<doc id="2061" url="https://su.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=2061" title="Reliability modelling">
Reliability modelling

<ol>
<li>ALIH</<li>
</ol>
Two separate fields of investigation are common.
The &lt;a href="physics%20of%20failure"&gt;physics of failure&lt;/a&gt; approach uses an understanding of the failure mechanisms involved, such as &lt;a href="crack%20propagation"&gt;crack propagation&lt;/a&gt; or chemical &lt;a href="corrosion"&gt;corrosion&lt;/a&gt;.
The &lt;a href="parts%20stress%20modelling"&gt;parts stress modelling&lt;/a&gt; approach is an empirical method for prediction based on counting the number and type of components of the system, and the stress they undergo during operation.

